        "original_id": "879d007e-b0eb-5d09-984a-29361aa1f5a9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: UNLV Runnin' Rebels, University of Nevada, Las Vegas, Duke\n- People: Jerry Tarkanian, Anderson Hunt, Bobby Hurley\n- Events: 1990–91 NCAA Division I men's basketball season, 1991 NCAA tournament, national semifinal\n- Topics: defending national champions, unbeaten regular season\n\nFacts:\n- The 1990–91 UNLV Runnin' Rebels basketball team represented the University of Nevada, Las Vegas in NCAA Division I men's competition during the 1990–91 season.\n- Jerry Tarkanian, born on August 8, 1930, was an American basketball coach.\n- The UNLV Runnin' Rebels, coached by Jerry Tarkanian, entered the 1990–91 season as defending national champions.\n- The UNLV Runnin' Rebels entered the 1991 NCAA tournament unbeaten.\n- In the 1991 national semifinal, the UNLV Runnin' Rebels lost to eventual champion Duke after Anderson Hunt's final-seconds three-point attempt bounced off the backboard into the hands of Duke player Bobby Hurley.\n- The 1990–91 UNLV Runnin' Rebels were the last team to finish the regular season unbeaten until St. Joseph's did so in 2004.\n- Jerry Tarkanian died on February 11, 2015.",
